KUF port M13: upload buffer pages (shared memory uploads, constants, converted vertex and index data) are placed in
device-local host-visible memory on discrete GPUs whose host-visible device-local heap is at least 1 GiB (resizable
BAR), instead of system memory: about 21 MB of shared memory uploads per frame at 4K were copied over PCIe by the GPU.
Integrated GPUs (the Steam Deck) and small BAR windows keep the old choice. --vulkan_upload_device_local=false
restores it.
